// frontseat.runner.v1alpha1: what a worker's runner is told to start for a
// test. It is no API: nothing serves it and no client asks it. It is a
// file the daemon writes and the runner reads, both of this server, and
// its Go is theirs alone (server/internal/runnerapi).
//
// It lists every service a test needs, those its services need
// included, and which of their ports the test and each service may
// reach. The worker's runner makes a sandbox for the test and one for
// each service, each with a loopback of its own and no other network.
// The daemon has already worked out what to start, from the Resources
// the test's Component depends on and the APIs it consumes. It writes
// the file into the action's input root, at
// .frontseat/runtime/runner.binpb, so that it is part of the action's
// digest and nothing outside the Remote Execution API carries it; the
// runner reads it there.

